    add("th2-memory-map", "", "Handbook: Chapter 1: MSX system overview", "", "Memory map: The MSX2 has three kinds of memory: MAIN-ROM, SUB-ROM, and RAM. Each memory...",
        R"MAN(LIVRO: MSX2 Technical Handbook (ASCII Corporation, 1987)
CAPITULO: Chapter 1: MSX system overview

The MSX2 has three kinds of memory: MAIN-ROM, SUB-ROM, and RAM. Each memory resides in an independent 64K address space and is allocated as shown in Figure 1.4 (1) (each 64K space is called a "slot", which consists of four 16K areas called "pages"). Figures 1.3 (2) and (3) show memory usage when using BASIC and MSX-DOS, respectively.

For each class of memory, Figure 1.5 shows the memory map of Figure 1.4 (1)(a), Figure 1.6 for Figure 1.4 (1)(b), and Figure 1.7 for Figure 1.4 (1)(c). There is also a [VRAM map](Appendix5.md) and [I/O map](Appendix6.md) whose standards are defined. They are found in the APPENDIX.

FONTE
  MSX2 Technical Handbook (ASCII Corporation, 1987); texto em ingles, como no original.)MAN");

