    add("th2-escape-sequence", "", "Handbook: Chapter 2: BASIC", "", "Escape sequence: MSX has the escape sequence feature (see [Appendix...",
        R"MAN(LIVRO: MSX2 Technical Handbook (ASCII Corporation, 1987)
CAPITULO: Chapter 2: BASIC

MSX has the escape sequence feature (see [Appendix 10](Appendices8and10.md#appendix-10---escape-sequences)), which can be used in the PRINT statement of BASIC, and in console output of BIOS or BDOS call (MSX-DOS). The escape sequence feature is a subset of DEC VT52 terminal and Heathkit H19 terminal.

FONTE
  MSX2 Technical Handbook (ASCII Corporation, 1987); texto em ingles, como no original.)MAN");

    add("th2-returning-to-basic", "", "Handbook: Chapter 2: BASIC", "", "Returning to BASIC: _Warm start_",
        R"MAN(LIVRO: MSX2 Technical Handbook (ASCII Corporation, 1987)
CAPITULO: Chapter 2: BASIC

_Warm start_

After selecting a slot of MAIN-ROM, jump to 409BH of MAIN-ROM. If the work area of BASIC has not been destroyed, the BASIC prompt will be displayed. The contents of register and stack at the jump are ignored.

Another way is to execute the next command in internal routine NEWSTT (see [4.4 of Chapter 2](Chapter2.md#44-expansion-of-cmd-command)) (see Figure 2.20)

FONTE
  MSX2 Technical Handbook (ASCII Corporation, 1987); texto em ingles, como no original.)MAN");

