    add("th2-pattern-name-table-6", "", "Handbook: Chapter 4: VDP and display screen (1-5)", "", "Pattern name table: In GRAPHIC 4 mode, one byte of the pattern name table corresponds...",
        R"MAN(LIVRO: MSX2 Technical Handbook (ASCII Corporation, 1987)
CAPITULO: Chapter 4: VDP and display screen (1-5)

In GRAPHIC 4 mode, one byte of the pattern name table corresponds with 2 dots on the screen. The colour information of each dot is represented by 4 bits and 16 colours can be specified (see Figure 4.37). The starting address of the pattern name table is specified by R#2. Only the 2 high order bits of the address (A16 to A15) are specified and the 15 low order bits are considered as "0". Thus, the four addresses at which the pattern name can be set are 00000H, 08000H, 10000H, and 18000H.

FONTE
  MSX2 Technical Handbook (ASCII Corporation, 1987); texto em ingles, como no original.)MAN");

    add("th2-figure-4-37-pattern-name-table-structure-of-graphic-4-mode", "", "Handbook: Chapter 4: VDP and display screen (1-5)", "", "_Figure 4.37 Pattern name table structure of GRAPHIC 4 mode_: The dot at (X,Y) coordinate...",
        R"MAN(LIVRO: MSX2 Technical Handbook (ASCII Corporation, 1987)
CAPITULO: Chapter 4: VDP and display screen (1-5)

[Ver Figura: Figure 4.37]

The dot at (X,Y) coordinate on the screen can be accessed by using Expression 4.1. The program of List 4.2 illustrates the use of Expression 4.1.

FONTE
  MSX2 Technical Handbook (ASCII Corporation, 1987); texto em ingles, como no original.)MAN");

    add("th2-expression-4-1-the-expression-for-accessing-the-dot-at-x-y-c", "", "Handbook: Chapter 4: VDP and display screen (1-5)", "", "_Expression 4.1 The expression for accessing the dot at (X,Y) coordinate_: (The colour of...",
        R"MAN(LIVRO: MSX2 Technical Handbook (ASCII Corporation, 1987)
CAPITULO: Chapter 4: VDP and display screen (1-5)

        ADR = X/2 + Y * 128 + base address

(The colour of the dot is represented by 4 high order bits in the case that X is even and by 4 low order bits in the case that X is odd.)

FONTE
  MSX2 Technical Handbook (ASCII Corporation, 1987); texto em ingles, como no original.)MAN");

    add("th2-list-4-2-pset-for-graphic-4-mode-written-in-basic", "", "Handbook: Chapter 4: VDP and display screen (1-5)", "", "_List 4.2 PSET for GRAPHIC 4 mode written in BASIC_",
        R"MAN(LIVRO: MSX2 Technical Handbook (ASCII Corporation, 1987)
CAPITULO: Chapter 4: VDP and display screen (1-5)

    100 '*
    110 '  LIST 4.2   dot access of GRAPHIC 4 mode
    120 '*
    130 '
    140 SCREEN 5
    150 BA=0
    160 FOR I=0 TO 255
    170   X=I:Y=I\2
    180   COL=15
    190   GOSUB 1000
    200 NEXT
    210 END
    220 '
    1000 '
    1010 '  PSET (X,Y),COL
    1020 '   COL:color  BA:graphics Base Address
    1030 '
    1040 '
    1050 ADR=X\2+Y*128+BA
    1060 IF X AND 1 THEN BIT=&HF0:C=COL ELSE BIT=&HF:C=COL*16
    1070 D=VPEEK(ADR)
    1080 D=(D AND BIT) OR C
    1090 VPOKE ADR,D
    1100 RETURN

FONTE
  MSX2 Technical Handbook (ASCII Corporation, 1987); texto em ingles, como no original.)MAN");

