    add("th2-6-7-register-status-at-command-termination", "", "Handbook: Chapter 4: VDP and display screen (6)", "", "6.7 Register Status at Command Termination: Table 4.7 shows the register status at the...",
        R"MAN(LIVRO: MSX2 Technical Handbook (ASCII Corporation, 1987)
CAPITULO: Chapter 4: VDP and display screen (6)

Table 4.7 shows the register status at the command termination for each command.

When the number of dots to be executed in Y direction assumes N, the values of SY*, DY*, and NYB can be calculated as follows:

        SY*=SY+N, DY*=DY+N .................... when DIY bit is 0
        SY*=SY-N, DY*=DY-N .................... when DIY bit is 1
        NYB=NY-N

*Note:* when MAJ bit is 0 in LINE, N = N - 1.

FONTE
  MSX2 Technical Handbook (ASCII Corporation, 1987); texto em ingles, como no original.)MAN");

